  "notes": "A strong verb describing aggressive verbal abuse — shouting insults, cursing, or berating someone loudly. Implies sustained, vociferous abuse rather than a single remark. Literary in tone but understood in everyday Japanese.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {罵|ののし}り{合|あ}う: to hurl insults at each other\n- {大声|おおごえ}で{罵|ののし}る: to shout abuse\n- {罵|ののし}り{続|つづ}ける: to keep hurling insults\n- {口汚|くちぎたな}く{罵|ののし}る: to abuse in foul language\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {怒鳴|どな}る: to shout, to yell (angry shouting, not necessarily with insults)\n- {罵倒|ばとう}する: to denounce, to vilify (more formal, written)\n- {悪口|わるくち}を{言|い}う: to speak ill of, to badmouth (milder, can be behind someone's back)\n- {詰|なじ}る: to reproach, to rebuke (implies blaming rather than raw abuse)",
